  "description": "SAN DIEGO - A Coast Guard MH-60T Jayhawk helicopter crew airlifted a man who severely injured his hand aboard the commercial fishing vessel Intrepid, Monday, Sept. 26, 2011.   Flying as cover, a C-130 Hercules airplane from Coast Guard Air Station Sacramento, Calif., also responded, while the helicopter traveled 225 miles to retrieve the man and deliver him to a waiting ambulance bound for U.C. San Diego Medical Center for treatment. U.S. Coast Guard video by Air Station Sacramento.",
